{"id": "EUVD-2026-102333", "enisaUuid": "f4e07cd4-9cb2-338b-ac2e-1e401a6550e3", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a configuration injection vulnerability that allows authenticated WebGUI users to inject mpd5 commands by submitting an unescaped RADIUS shared secret. Attackers with L2TP or PPPoE Server edit privileges can POST a secret containing a quote and newline to vpn_l2tp.php or services_pppoe_edit.php, appending an up-script that executes as root when a session starts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:46:21", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-l2tp-radius-mpd", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/vpn.inc#L428-L441", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/vpn.inc#L202-L215", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/vpn_l2tp.php#L137-L143", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-command-injection-via-radius-secret-mpd-conf-injection"], "aliases": ["GHSA-28v9-q2x4-wjw8", "CVE-2026-111221"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.94, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5a169117-b9b9-3944-a997-f40af771188b", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d9159c44-a23a-346f-b487-be975f51ece3", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}